    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet well back from Leeson Street close to the junction with Waterloo Road, with off street car parking for several cars, this attractive, three storey over basement townhouse epitomizes the character and gracious proportions synonymous with the Georgian era. Although requiring refurbishment, the property retains many fine original period features including a stunning and unique stained glass window on the half landing, marble fireplaces, sash windows and ornate ceiling cornices making it the perfect choice for those wishing to create a stunningly elegant town residence.\n\nThe property has most recently been laid out as an investment property with four apartments, one being on each floor. Subject to planning, the house will easily reconvert back into a spacious family home with a suggested layout comprising of entrance hall, sitting room, dining room, drawing room, kitchen, 4 bedrooms with a number of bathrooms. There would also be a self-contained apartment at basement level.\n\nThe property benefits from an exceptionally convenient location close to the junction of Waterloo Road ensuring a superb choice of amenities are within a pleasant stroll including local shopping on Leeson Street and Baggot Street, not to mention Donnybrook Fair in Donnybrook village, Ballsbridge and Ranelagh Villages. St Stephen's Green is also within walking distance. Recreational amenities close by include the Aviva stadium, Herbert Park, Fitzwilliam Lawn tennis club, and the RDS. Many of Dublin's principal places of business such as Merrion Square, Fitzwilliam Square and Ballsbridge are also within a short stroll as are some of the city's premier schools such as St Conleths, Loreto on the Green, Sandford Park, Gonzaga college and Muckross Park."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nwith ceiling cornice, centre rose, original fan light and original arch.\n\nSitting Room: - \nwith sash window overlooking the front garden, ceiling cornice, centre rose and original fireplace with cast-iron inset. Folding doors to:\n\nDining Room: - \nwith sash window overlooking the garden, ceiling cornice, centre rose and steps to:\n\nRear Hall: with door to the garden. - \n\n\nKitchenette: - \nwith fitted units, electric hob, oven, extractor fan and tiled splashback.\n\nHALL FLOOR RETURN - \n\n\nLanding: - \nwith a stunning stained glass window and original detailed wall cornicing.\n\nFIRST FLOOR - \n\n\nDrawing Room: - \nspanning the full width of the house with intricate ceiling cornice, centre rose, two sash windows with shutters and a stunning marble fireplace.\n\nBedroom 1: - \noverlooking the rear garden with ceiling cornice and original fireplace.\n\nFIRST FLOOR RETURN - \n\n\nShower Room: - \nwith wc, wash hand basin and step-in shower.\n\nSECOND FLOOR - \n\n\nBedroom 2: - \nwith ceiling cornice, original fireplace and sash window with shutters.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nwith ceiling cornice, original fireplace and sash window with shutters.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nwith ceiling cornice and sash window with shutters.\n\nTOP FLOOR RETURN - \n\n\nShower Room: - \nwith original porthole window, wc, wash hand basin and step-in shower.\n\nBASEMENT LEVEL - \n\n\nSelf Contained Apartment: - \nSpacious apartment needing refurbishment or integration into the upper floors, subject to planning permission.\n\n"
      },
